THOUGHT: I’ll fix one NullAway error by ensuring `GuiComponent.getFont()` never returns null. A common pattern is to lazily initialize the font to a default when it’s null, then return it. This avoids changing callers and satisfies the non-null contract. After editing, I’ll rerun the build to confirm the total NullAway error count drops from 6 to 5 and that no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '227,229c\  public Font getFont() {
    if (this.font == null) {
      this.font = new Font(Font.DIALOG, Font.PLAIN, 12);
    }

    return this.font;
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/gui/GuiComponent.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 120 new_build_output.log
```

